<title>USA: D&amp;P rates Central Bank of Philippines issue 'BB'.</title>
<headline>D&amp;P rates Central Bank of Philippines issue 'BB'.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Tuesday it assigned a double-B rating with a positive outlook to the forthcoming Yankee bond issue of the Central Bank of the Philippines.</p>
<p>The issue is expected to be launched in two tranches, a 30-year tranche of US$500 million and a 100-year tranche of US$250 million.</p>
<p>Duff said it may raise its rating on the issue, reflecting the success of the Philippines in managing its economy. Further improvement in the country's fiscal profile and in credit quality are related to the passage of forthcoming tax reform legislation, it added.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
